# Substrate terminfo database

Source: etc/termcap (BSD-style termcap with 4 entries — vt100,
ansi, linux, substrate).  Compiled to the standard terminfo binary
format via:

    captoinfo ../termcap > substrate.ti
    tic -o ../terminfo substrate.ti

The compiled entries live at ../terminfo/{a,l,s,v}/* and are
installed by build-rootfs.sh into both /etc/terminfo/ (via the
generic etc/ copy) and /usr/share/terminfo/ (canonical location
ncurses-style consumers check first).

## Coverage

  - vt100, vt100-am  — generic DEC VT100 with auto-margin
  - ansi             — ANSI/PC-term with 16-color extension
  - linux            — Linux console (matches what the substrate
                       kernel exports for its text VT)
  - substrate        — alias for linux

## Caveat (2026)

zsh / less / vi look up terminfo via setupterm(), which calls
into the libcurses on the system.  Substrate currently ships a
stub libcurses (lib/curses/) — every setupterm returns -1, every
tigetstr returns the "absent" sentinel.  So shipping these
binary entries is a no-op for now; they only become live once we
port a real terminfo backend (the obvious option is NetBSD's
libterminfo, ~5 KLOC).

The binaries are still worth committing today because the
*format* doesn't change with the runtime port — when we wire up
real terminfo resolution later, these entries will Just Work.
